An editor of source code: a real <textarea> (typing, IME, the undo of the browser, screen readers and mobile keyboards work as in any field) over a layer that draws the text highlighted by the Syntax Service. It has no toolbar: the controls of an Application call its methods (the ready event gives the editor). - Value, Language (a language of the Syntax Service), LineNumbers, Wrap, TabSize, Spaces (indents with spaces, not tabs), Pairs (closes brackets and quotes), ActiveLine, ReadOnly, Disabled, Invalid, Placeholder, Name, Label; Rows (the lines it shows) or AutoSize (grows with the text). - Markers: [{Line, Column, EndLine, EndColumn, Severity, Message}] underline the text (lines and columns from 1; without Column the whole line; without an end the word). Severity: error, warning or info. The pointer over a marker shows its message. - Complete(context, callback) offers completions as the user types a word (and on Ctrl+Space): context is {Text, Offset, Line, Column, Word, Before, Language, Explicit}; callback(error, items), items [{Label, Insert, Detail, Kind}] or texts. The items that start with the word show; Enter or Tab inserts one. - Hint(context, callback) shows a hint for the text under the pointer: callback(error, text). - Keys: Tab and Shift+Tab indent and outdent (Escape, then Tab, leaves the editor), Enter keeps the indent, Mod+/ comments the lines, Mod+] and Mod+[ indent and outdent, Ctrl+Space completes, Mod+F finds and Mod+R (or Mod+H) replaces in its own find bar (a FindBar over its corner; FindBar: false leaves it to the page). - Methods: Focus(), Selection() ({Start, End, Text}), Select(start, end), Insert(text), Replace(start, end, text), Position(offset) ({Line, Column}), Offset(line, column), GoTo(line, column), Undo(), Redo(), Indent(), Outdent(), Comment(), Find(query, {Case, Word, RegExp}) (returns the count of matches and selects the next one), FindNext(), FindPrevious(), ReplaceCurrent(text), ReplaceAll(text), ClearFind(), Print(options, callback) (the Print Service; options as there). - Diff view: with Original (the text before) and Diff 'unified' (one column; true too) or 'split' (the two texts side by side), the editor shows how Value differs from Original, read only: the lines removed and added on their colors, the words changed inside a changed line marked, the numbers of the lines in both texts, highlighted as in the editing view; the unchanged runs fold down to Context lines (3) around the changes, and a press on a fold opens it. DiffStats() returns {Added, Removed}; NextChange() and PreviousChange() scroll to a change. - Events: input and change (Value), cursor ({Line, Column, Start, End}), ready (the editor). Properties | Property | Default | | --- | --- | | Value | '' | | Language | 'text' | | LineNumbers | true | | Wrap | false | | TabSize | 4 | | Spaces | false | | Pairs | true | | ActiveLine | true | | ReadOnly | false | | Disabled | false | | Invalid | false | | Placeholder | '' | | Name | null | | Label | '' | | Rows | 12 | | AutoSize | false | | Markers | [] | | Complete | null | | Hint | null | | Original | null | | Diff | false | | Context | 3 | | FindBar | true | Events - ready: The editor is ready: the component itself, to call its methods. - cursor: The caret or the selection moved: {Line, Column, Start, End}. - input: The code changed while typing: Value. - change: The code was committed when the focus left: Value. - complete: A completion was accepted: the item chosen. Methods - Indent() - Outdent() - Comment() - Focus() - Selection() - Select(start, end) - Insert(text) - Replace(start, end, text) - Position(offset) - Offset(line, column) - GoTo(line, column) - Undo() - Redo() - Find(query, options) - FindNext() - FindPrevious() - ReplaceCurrent(text) - ReplaceAll(text) - ClearFind() - Print(options, callback) - DiffStats() - NextChange() - PreviousChange() Example <RadioGroup Variant="segmented" [options]="[{Value: 'javascript', Label: 'JavaScript'}, {Value: 'python', Label: 'Python'}, {Value: 'sql', Label: 'SQL'}]" [value]="Language" (change)="Chose" /> <CodeEditor [language]="Language" [value]="Code" LineNumbers="true" Rows="8" Pairs="true" (input)="Typed" (cursor)="Moved" /> <p class="elemenx-text small muted">{{Code.length}} characters · {{Cursor}} · Mod+F finds, Mod+H replaces, Mod+/ comments a line.</p> <script> ({ Language: 'javascript', Cursor: '', Code: "/ A counter. /
function count (limit) {
	var total = 0;

	for (var i = 0; i < limit; i++)
		total += i;

	return total;
}
", Samples: { javascript: "/ A counter. /
function count (limit) {
	var total = 0;

	for (var i = 0; i < limit; i++)
		total += i;

	return total;
}
", python: "def count(limit):
	"""A counter."""
	return sum(range(limit)) # the total
", sql: "SELECT name, COUNT() AS orders
FROM users
GROUP BY name;
" }, Chose: function (value) { this.Language = value; this.Code = this.Samples[value]; }, Typed: function (value) { this.Code = value; }, Moved: function (cursor) { this.Cursor = 'line ' + cursor.Line + ', column ' + cursor.Column; } }) </script>

Source code shown, not edited: Value highlighted by the Syntax Service in Language, as a CodeEditor draws it. LineNumbers (and Start, the number of the first line), Wrap, Highlight ([3, '7-9']: lines marked), Copy (a button that copies the code, on by default), Label. The text is selectable; Rows limits its height in lines (it scrolls). Fold: a bracket ({, [ or () that closes on a later line, or an element of HTML or XML whose closing tag is on a later line (<ul> ... </ul>; not one that closes itself, nor a void element), makes a block that folds: a button beside its first line hides the lines up to the one that closes it, and the first line ends with … and the rest of that last one ("items": [ … ], or <ul> … </ul>). A press on … unfolds it too. Folded lists the numbers of the lines whose blocks start folded; the event fold reports {Line, Folded} at each press. Without Value the code is the body of the element (<CodeView Language="html">&lt;p&gt;Hi&lt;/p&gt;</CodeView>: its text, so a tag in it is written as &lt;), without the indentation its lines share: the body follows its changes. Properties | Property | Default | | --- | --- | | Value | '' | | Language | 'text' | | LineNumbers | false | | Start | 1 | | Wrap | false | | Highlight | [] | | Copy | true | | Rows | 0 | | Label | '' | | Fold | false | | Folded | [] | Events - fold: A block was folded or unfolded: {Line, Folded}. Slots default Example <CodeView Language="javascript" LineNumbers="true" [highlight]="[4]" Label="A function" Value="function greet (name) {&#10;&#9;var text = 'Hello, ' + name;&#10;&#10;&#9;return text.toUpperCase();&#10;}" /> <CodeView Language="json" Fold="true" [folded]="[7]" Label="A package" [value]="Package" (fold)="Folded" /> <p class="elemenx-text small muted">{{Note}}</p> <CodeView Language="css" Rows="3" Value=".card {&#10;&#9;color: var(--elemenx-accent);&#10;&#9;padding: 12px;&#10;&#9;border-radius: 8px;&#10;}" /> <script> ({ Note: 'Fold: the arrows fold the blocks, … unfolds them; the copy button shows under the pointer.', Package: '{
	"name": "elemenx",
	"keywords": [
		"ui",
		"es5"
	],
	"scripts": {
		"test": "vitest",
		"lint": "eslint ."
	}
}
', Folded: function (event) { this.Note = 'Line ' + event.Line + (event.Folded ? ' folded' : ' unfolded'); } }) </script> Tests - writes the text of a Markdown and the code of a CodeView as their body, edited in a field of many lines — tests/examples/designer.spec.js

The differences between two texts, to read (the Diff Service): Before and After, line by line, with the words that changed marked in a line changed. Mode: unified (the lines removed then the ones added, one column) or split (the text before on the left, the text after on the right). Context lines around each change (3); the unchanged runs between them fold, and a press on a fold shows it. The header counts the lines added and removed, with Title (a name of a file). LineNumbers shows the numbers of each side. Properties | Property | Default | | --- | --- | | Before | '' | | After | '' | | Mode | 'unified' | | Context | 3 | | LineNumbers | true | | Title | '' | Example <DiffView Title="sum.js" [before]="Before" [after]="After" [mode]="Mode" Context="1" /> <RadioGroup Variant="segmented" Label="Mode" [options]="[{Value: 'unified', Label: 'Unified'}, {Value: 'split', Label: 'Side by side'}]" [value]="Mode" (change)="Moded" /> <script> ({ Mode: 'unified', Before: 'function sum (list) {
	var total = 0;

	for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++)
		total += list[i];

	return total;
}

module.exports = sum;', After: 'function sum (list) {
	var total = 0;

	list.forEach(function (value) {
		total += value;
	});

	return total;
}

module.exports = sum;', Moded: function (value) { this.Mode = value; } }) </script> Tests - CastList, DiffView, MediaHero, MediaShelf and VideoTimeline are as wide as a column of flex-start — tests/regression/inline-size-width.test.js - DiffView shows the lines removed and added with the words that changed, folds the unchanged runs and opens them — tests/regression/library-new.test.js

The highlighting of source code: the grammars of the languages and the tokens of a text in one of them. Built in: javascript (js, mjs, cjs, jsx), typescript (ts, tsx), json, html (xml, svg), css, markdown (md), sql, python (py), shell (sh, bash, zsh), yaml (yml), toml, ini (cfg, conf, properties, env) and csv (tsv); text has no rules. Used by CodeEditor; any component may show highlighted code with it. - Register(name, grammar) adds a language (or replaces one): {Aliases, Rules, Comment, Indent}. Rules are [Type, RegExp, Options]: the first rule that matches nearest wins (a rule must not match empty text). Type is the class of the token (elemenx-syntax-<Type>; null for plain text). Options: Inside (a language name, or a function (match) returning one: the match is read in that language) or Groups (the types of the capture groups, which follow each other and cover the match; a group may be {Inside}). Comment: {Line: '//'} or {Block: ['<!--', '-->']} for the comment command of an editor. Indent: a RegExp of the text before a line break that indents the next line one more step. - Find(name) returns the grammar of a language or of an alias (null when there is none); Languages() the names. - Tokens(text, language) returns [{Type, Text}] covering the text; Lines(text, language) the same split into lines (a token never holds a line break); HTML(text, language) escaped markup with a span for each token. Methods - Register(name, grammar) - Find(name) - Languages() - Tokens(text, language) - Lines(text, language) - HTML(text, language) Example <Select [options]="Languages" [value]="Language" (change)="Chose" /> <pre class="elemenx-code" [property.innerHTML]="Html(Sample, Language)"></pre> <p class="elemenx-text small muted">{{Count(Sample, Language)}} tokens</p> <script> ({ Language: 'javascript', Sample: "// A sum
function add (a, b) {
	return a + b 2; / twice /
}
", Languages: [{Value: 'javascript', Label: 'JavaScript'}, {Value: 'python', Label: 'Python'}, {Value: 'sql', Label: 'SQL'}], Samples: { javascript: "// A sum
function add (a, b) {
	return a + b 2; / twice /
}
", python: "def add(a, b):
	"""A sum."""
	return a + b 2 # twice
", sql: "SELECT name, COUNT() AS orders
FROM users
WHERE active = 1
GROUP BY name;
" }, $OnCreate: function () { var syntax = this.$Service('Syntax'); this.Html = function (text, language) { return syntax.HTML(text, language); }; this.Count = function (text, language) { return syntax.Tokens(text, language).length; }; }, Chose: function (value) { this.Language = value; this.Sample = this.Samples[value]; } }) </script> Tests - covers the whole text with its tokens in every language — tests/regression/syntax.test.js - reads YAML, TOML, INI and CSV: their keys, sections, strings, numbers, anchors and comments — tests/regression/syntax.test.js - reads JavaScript: comments, strings, regular expressions, numbers, keywords and calls — tests/regression/syntax.test.js - reads a block comment and a string left open up to the end, as they are typed — tests/regression/syntax.test.js - reads the script and the style of HTML in their languages, and the tags and attributes — tests/regression/syntax.test.js - reads the code of a fenced block of Markdown in the language it names — tests/regression/syntax.test.js - splits the tokens into lines, one array for each line — tests/regression/syntax.test.js - escapes the HTML it returns — tests/regression/syntax.test.js - finds languages by their aliases and takes new ones — tests/regression/syntax.test.js
